set(s for b in bs for s in b['source_ids']))))\ndef path(ex,ids,fs,ss): return dict(explanation=ex,behavior_ids=ids.split(),fact_ids=fs.split(),source_ids=ss.split())\noverview=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation, authority transition, old-work handling and necessary membership/recovery/application support have been traced. Local discrepancies and deeper variants remain explicitly open.',formation=path('The elected leader stamps and persists commands, then reports its local match and notifies peer replicators. Sender-bounded AppendEntries and snapshot success report matching indexes to a tenure-local commitment object, which includes only latest-configuration voters. Its majority order statistic advances only through the current-term startIndex. A main-loop notification consumes that index, commits membership and enqueues ordered FSM work; follower append handling propagates leader commitment after prefix checks and conflict replacement. runFSM resolves command futures after callbacks, while log dispatch watermarks precede callback completion.','B-replicate B-quorum B-commit-consume B-fsm','F-quorum-index','M-apply M-commit M-send M-reply M-update M-follower M-leader-loop M-fsm M-fsm-rest'),context=path('Normal timeout candidacy requires local voter eligibility. Optional pre-vote precedes term persistence, self-vote and requests only to voters. Recipients enforce candidate membership, term, prior vote and last-log freshness; request-specific response channels and majority tally acquire leadership. Transfers catch up a target then send TimeoutNow, whose election bypasses pre-vote/known-leader rejection but still tallies votes. Incoming qualifying terms, higher-term replication replies, lease loss and committed self-removal end a tenure. Old replication callbacks retain old commitment/stepDown objects; cleanup stops workers, fails remaining inflight/verification futures and discards tenure fields. Already queued FSM work can still complete. Network heartbeat fast-path carries no entries or commitment and may run concurrently.','B-election B-tenure B-transfer B-transport B-verify-start B-verify-support B-verify-finish','F-verify-support','M-election M-vote M-elect-send M-leader M-leader-loop M-transfer M-timeout-now M-lease M-net-dispatch'),connection=path('Persistent vote/term and log freshness constrain subsequent authority acquisition; durable log entries survive tenure loss although their uncommitted futures fail. Each new leader resets volatile match evidence and appends a current-term noop before advancing old-history commitment. Configuration admission waits for both stable membership and current-term commitment, then changes the support electorate; suffix replacement can roll latest membership back. Snapshot capture includes applied history plus committed configuration, and restart/install reconstruct history and membership before participation/catch-up. Verification is a separate authority-support path: its threshold counts voters, but notification registration spans all replicators. That discrepancy is retained without equating callback count with legitimate authority.','B-election B-tenure B-membership B-history B-resync B-quorum B-verify-start B-verify-support','F-quorum-index F-verify-support','M-durable M-restart M-snapshot-build M-install M-snapshot-send M-commit M-leader M-verify M-notify'),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Verification eligibility and callback timing relative to election/lease expiry.','Legal sender history for follower commitment beyond the current validated request prefix.','Partial-store-error recovery after conflict truncation; delayed snapshots; manual Restore and forced RecoverCluster paths.','Transport-specific pipeline ordering and error behavior beyond representative dispatch.'])\nsurfaces=[dict(entry_point='Raft.VerifyLeader / Raft.verifyLeader',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-verify-start','B-verify-support','B-verify-finish'],reason='Voter-derived threshold versus all-replicator support is a selected unresolved discrepancy.',source_ids=['M-verify','M-verify-api','M-notify'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries follower commit propagation',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-commit-consume'],reason='Local log cap differs from current request prefix; sender backtracking may exclude the suspected divergent-suffix history and must be investigated.',source_ids=['M-follower','M-send','M-reply'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries StoreLogs failure after DeleteRange',disposition='deferred',reason='Explicit stale last-log metadata TODO after failed replacement; fault contract and recovery paths not yet established.',source_ids=['M-follower'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.restoreUserSnapshot / RecoverCluster',disposition='deferred',reason='Manual destructive history replacement differs from ordinary consensus recovery; inspect caller contract before treating it as a fault.',source_ids=['M-client'],high_consequence=True)]\nmapdoc=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured HashiCorp raft Go module: core Raft goroutines, configuration, log/snapshot orchestration, FSM dispatch and transport interfaces. Injected storage/FSM/transport implementations retain caller duties; in-repository implementations are not externalized.',protocol_contexts=['Raft term and local role','Leadership tenure commitment object','Latest/committed membership indexes','Per-operation apply/verify futures'],external_interfaces=['FSM','LogStore','StableStore','SnapshotStore','Transport','Apply/Barrier/VerifyLeader/Shutdown'],ownership=['Main loop owns protocol configuration and role-driven dispatch; peer replication workers own RPC progression; runFSM owns application ordering.'],source_ids=['M-restart','M-transport','M-client','M-consume']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=facts,surfaces=surfaces,core_overview=overview)\njson.dump(mapdoc,open('map-01.json','w'),indent=2)\nquestion=dict(question='Can VerifyLeader consume successful notifications from nonvoters as sufficient authority support, and thereby return success when the local peer can no longer safely serve the API’s promised leadership check?',importance='Incorrect success can authorize stale FSM reads after another voter majority acquires authority; the local eligibility/accounting discrepancy matters even before a wider read witness is constructed.',source_ids=['M-verify-api','M-verify','M-verify-vote','M-notify','M-heartbeat','M-lease','M-suffrage','M-leader-loop'],participants=['leader','voting followers','nonvoting replication peers','VerifyLeader caller'],objects=['verifyFuture','replication notify maps','configuration electorate'],contexts=['Established leadership with mixed voter/nonvoter membership','Verification interval with unavailable voter responses'],event_paths=['VerifyLeader -> verifyCh -> verifyLeader -> all replication notify maps -> heartbeat/append/snapshot response -> notifyAll -> vote -> verifyCh -> leaderLoop result'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-verify-start','B-verify-support','B-verify-finish'],fact_ids=['F-verify-support'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-membership':'Defines voter/nonvoter eligibility and all-peer replication population.','B-tenure':'Lease and term-driven stepdown can reject pending verification.','B-election':'A separate voter majority can acquire authority; legal timing is to be reconstructed.','B-client':'API return and future completion distinguish admission from observed success.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Lease checks count only voters and can terminate old leadership independently.','Higher-term append/snapshot replies schedule failure/stepdown; recipients reject stale-term heartbeats.','Suffrage interface explicitly discusses election and commitment, not verification; API and composed authority mechanism must ground verification responsibility.'],unknowns=['Does the API’s authority-check responsibility exclude success based solely on self plus nonvoters, and what exact local or cluster history grounds that implication?','Can an actual legal transport/election schedule retain old-leader belief long enough for nonvoter notifications to produce a completed success after authority is lost?','Which observation boundary cleanly distinguishes lack of admitted voter support from unrecorded earlier notifications?'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Read producer-to-consumer path shows identity-free votes from every replication worker, unlike voter-only lease and commitment paths. Next investigate the smallest lawful history and obligation before an expensive full-cluster test.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\njson.dump(dict(action='continue',rationale='Register the first sourced authority-support question alongside a usable two-core overview; preserve separate unresolved follower/history surfaces.',sources=sources,map_path='map-01.json',question=question),open('submission-02.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_map.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission-02.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"213c8068eec74675868f6d69ce1af9d8\", \"audit_spec_version\": 0, \"elapsed_seconds\": 220.20058887800042, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"core_overview\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [\"/core_overview/context/source_ids\"], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"Cite the referenced Behavior and Fact sources; labels alone do not explain a path\", \"allowed\": [\"read\", \"semantic_revision\"]}, {\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"submission\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [], \"material_ids\"